  "youtube_title": "Why AI Generated Frontend Code Always Looks the Same",
  "youtube_description": "AI coding agents suffer from a systemic design flaw: generic Inter fonts, identical purple-to-blue gradients, and repetitive nested cards. Enter Impeccable, an open-source deterministic engine that injects visual vocabulary, critique heuristics, and deterministic linter rules directly into agent harnesses like Claude Code, Cursor, and Codex CLI.\n\nChapters:\n0:00 - The AI Slop Problem\n0:12 - Why LLMs Default to Boring UI\n0:25 - Impeccable Architecture: 62 Deterministic Rules\n0:38 - Pre-commit Agent Hooks\n0:50 - Live Browser Hot-swapping\n1:03 - Benchmark: Deterministic Rules vs LLM Review\n1:17 - How to Ship Custom Brand Guardrails",
